window.products.push({"id":600241,"name":"Flexipan Madeleine 1.2 Oz, 78mm x 47mm x 19mm Deep (3-1/16\" x 1-13/16\" x 3/4\" Deep), 40 Cavities","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":157.7,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51NIXqZZGzL._AC_.jpg","description":"Flexipan 1511 fits in full-size (18 x 26) sheet pan. Flexipans have changed the way that pastry chefs work. The non stick flexible molds and trays do not have to be greased and will still unmold without breakage. The non stick quality also saves time and money. And because these flexible bakeware can be used at freezing temperatures, even frozen items such as ice cream, mousses, and aspics can be molded into any shape and be unmolded with ease. Flexipans are made with a combination of fiberglass and silicone. This allows the molds to be flexible, and gives them their non stick quality. The combination also gives the molds a longer life, making it possible to use them two or three thousand times before the first signs of sticking. The ease of cleaning also makes these flexible bakeware such a desirable tool. Our products conform to US regulations on food grade silicone, and are NSF and Kosher certified.FLEXIPAN Is Recognized By The Most Famous Chefs, Patissiers & Chefs de Cuisine Can Be Used Within The Same Heat Ranges As Ordinary Metal Baking Trays Or Pans (-40F To 536F) Freeze, Bake Or Microwave In The Same Mould A Must Have For Every Professional Chef FlexipanCare Instructions Handling Flexipan can be used from - 40 to 280C (-40 to 536F). Work with the Flexipan on a tray or any baking sheet. Check to ensure the Flexipan is dry and clean before placing any dough or batter in it. It can be used in all types of ovens and does not need to be greased the Flexipan is anti adherent by nature. De-panning Baked items: Remove the pieces one by one or by gently lifting the Flexipan to allow them to roll off the tray. Frozen items: Peel the item out of the molds. Frozen items must be depanned two to three minutes at the latest after comming out of the freezer. Cakes: For cake molds, turn the mold upside down. Large cakes, especially sponge cakes, should be allowed to cool before attempting to unmold. Maintenance and Care Wipe the Flexipan with a da","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51NIXqZZGzL._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Demarle","source_asin":"B000VDHAMM","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-600241","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B000VDHAMM","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B000VDHAMM","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
